1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,518
Brushing and flossing perfectly, but your gums still bleed?

2
00:00:03,838 --> 00:00:06,494
The cause might not be in your bathroom cabinet at all.

3
00:00:06,814 --> 00:00:17,703
Bleeding gums usually mean your immune system is fighting gumline inflammation - and three habits quietly fuel that: chronic stress, vaping, and not drinking enough water.

4
00:00:18,023 --> 00:00:19,381
First, chronic stress.

5
00:00:19,701 --> 00:00:27,058
It raises cortisol, weakening immune response and feeding inflammation - higher stress is linked to more plaque and more bleeding when you brush.

6
00:00:27,378 --> 00:00:28,546
Second, vaping.

7
00:00:28,866 --> 00:00:37,580
The aerosol disrupts bacteria in your mouth and ramps up inflammation at the gumline - research links vaping to more plaque and more bleeding on probing.

8
00:00:37,900 --> 00:00:39,564
Third, running low on water.

9
00:00:39,884 --> 00:00:46,175
Trading water for coffee and soda all day dries out your mouth, and less saliva means less protection for your gums.

10
00:00:46,495 --> 00:01:00,084
Try a short walk or deep breathing to ease stress, free quitline support like 1-800-QUIT-NOW can help if you vape, and keep water nearby to sip instead of coffee or soda.
